Specular patch to resvg 0.48.1 (src/image.rs, src/lib.rs): raster image hook.

What it changes
  Replaces the `raster-images` module (which decodes JPEG with zune-jpeg, PNG with
  tiny-skia's png codec, GIF with gif and WebP with image-webp) with a process-wide
  decoder hook: `resvg::set_raster_decoder(fn(&usvg::ImageKind) ->
  Option<Arc<tiny_skia::Pixmap>>)`. Drawing the decoded pixmap (pattern fill with the
  `image-rendering` filter quality) is upstream's code unchanged. Without a hook, raster
  images are skipped with a debug-level log record instead of a warning.

Why
  Specular decodes every raster format with its own in-tree decoders (and caches the result
  across renders, which upstream does not), and must not link third-party image decoders
  into the viewer. The `src/` directory is the published crate's with this patch applied;
  it is kept here as the record of the change.

